4\), so that \(\frac{3}{2}c' = \mathrm{g}' + 2\), but \(\frac{3}{2}c'\) is the perfect Fifth to *c'*, hence we must tune the required Fifth \(g' = \mathrm{g}' + 2\), that is, sharper than g' by 2 beats in a second. For the next Fifth in order to remain in the same @@L@@
